{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "newsletter_angle": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "One sentence on what ties this issue together"
    },
    "sections": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 2,
      "maxItems": 6,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "title": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Short, specific section heading"
          },
          "angle": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What this section tells the reader and why they care"
          },
          "search_query": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A web search query that finds evidence for this section"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "title",
          "angle",
          "search_query"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "newsletter_angle",
    "sections"
  ]
}

parameters.jsCode:
// Turns the plan into one item per section, capped at the number the form asked for
const brief = $('Read the brief').first().json;
const plan = $input.first().json.output || {};
const sections = Array.isArray(plan.sections) ? plan.sections.slice(0, brief.sections) : [];

if (!sections.length) {
  throw new Error('The planner returned no sections. Check the Claude credential and the "Plan the sections" output.');
}

return sections.map((s, i) => ({
  json: {
    index: i + 1,
    title: String(s.title || `Section ${i + 1}`).trim(),
    angle: String(s.angle || '').trim(),
    search_query: String(s.search_query || s.title || brief.topic).trim().slice(0, 300),
    newsletter_angle: plan.newsletter_angle || '',
  },
}));

parameters.text:
=Write one newsletter section.

Section: {{ $('Split into sections').item.json.title }}
Angle: {{ $('Split into sections').item.json.angle }}
Audience: {{ $('Read the brief').first().json.audience }}
Tone: {{ $('Read the brief').first().json.tone }}
Length: about {{ $('Read the brief').first().json.words_per_section }} words

Search results (the only facts you may use):
{{ ($json.results || []).map((r, i) => '[' + (i + 1) + '] ' + r.title + '\nURL: ' + r.url + '\n' + String(r.content || '').slice(0, 1500)).join('\n\n') || 'No results were found.' }}

Link each fact to the result it came from with <a href="URL">descriptive text</a>, using the exact URL above. If there are no results, write a short general section with no links and no statistics.

